<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bioko</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fernando Po, Fernando Póo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bioko, formerly Fernando Po, is a volcanic island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-guinea">Gulf of Guinea</a>, part of Equatorial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> and the site of its capital, Malabo. Spanish from 1778, it developed cocoa plantations that depended on contract labour from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>; a 1930 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> inquiry into the forced shipment of Liberian workers there brought down Liberia's president.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bioko.jpg" alt="Bioko" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bioko.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
